<article class="env-definition" id="07Y8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07Y8">Definition <span data-tag="07Y8">98.18.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a category fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. We say $\mathcal{X}$ satisfies <em>condition (RS*)</em> if given a fibre product diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ B' \ar[r] &  B \\  A' = A \times _ B B' \ar[u] \ar[r] &  A \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
  <p> of $S$-algebras, with $B' \to B$ surjective with square zero kernel, the functor of fibre categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{X}_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A')} \longrightarrow \mathcal{X}_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)} \times _{\mathcal{X}_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)}} \mathcal{X}_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B')}  \]
</div>
  <p> is an equivalence of categories. </p>
</article>